Z||000002||Old Lar||04-25-2001||10:17 PM||||You can get a sort of Carfax by logging on the web site and entering the VIN #. The report you ill get will tell you if the car has a clean title, but not all the details. To get the official Carfax report, you have to subscribe to the service for $20 or so for 3 months.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ken Wittlief||04-25-2001||10:54 PM||||Carfax will tell you the date a lein was recorded for the car in some states, but it wont tell you if the lein has been paid off or not.||||reg||1
Z||000004||EdsB52||04-25-2001||11:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Old Lar:<BR><B>You can get a sort of Carfax by logging on the web site and entering the VIN #. The report you ill get will tell you if the car has a clean title, but not all the details. To get the official Carfax report, you have to subscribe to the service for $20 or so for 3 months.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Been there done that, that's why I'm here. It's actually 20 bucks for 60 days. I just wondered if anyone is currently registered.<P>||||reg||1
